{
    "elements": [
        {
            "type": "ExpansionPanel",
            "name": "DocPanel",
            "caption": "📖 Documentation & help",
            "expanded": false,
            "items": [
                {
                    "type": "Label",
                    "caption": "── How it works ──"
                },
                {
                    "type": "Label",
                    "caption": "The tile is a standalone instance for the visualization, separate from the data connection: it reads its values from a StromGedachtWidget instance and updates immediately when something changes there. If there is exactly one StromGedachtWidget instance, it is detected automatically as the source – only with several do you have to choose manually below. Only what is enabled in the source is shown (StromGedacht, GrünstromIndex, Energy-Charts)."
                },
                {
                    "type": "Label",
                    "caption": "── Display ──"
                },
                {
                    "type": "Label",
                    "caption": "The traffic-light colors (super green/green/yellow/orange/red) apply uniformly to all three data sources. Surface, text and font options adapt the tile to your visualization; without your own setting the tile follows the light/dark design of the device. The tile name can be taken over from the source automatically. A tap on the 🔄 symbol updates the source immediately."
                },
                {
                    "type": "Label",
                    "caption": "── Automations ──"
                },
                {
                    "type": "Label",
                    "caption": "With 'Show automations' the tile fully manages the If→Then rules of the StromGedachtWidget source: '+ New rule' creates a rule, ✎ edits, the trash can deletes (with confirmation), the switch enables/disables. In the editor, switchable variables (with an action) are offered as targets – filterable by search field; for 'Set value' the values defined in the profile/presentation appear as a selection list. If the tile is linked several times, all changes act on the same rules everywhere."
                },
                {
                    "type": "Label",
                    "caption": "The button 'Reset colors & font to default' only changes the open form – it is saved only with 'Apply changes'."
                },
                {
                    "type": "Label",
                    "caption": "── More help ──"
                },
                {
                    "type": "Label",
                    "caption": "Detailed documentation: github.com/DG65/NRGStromGedachtWidget."
                },
                {
                    "type": "Label",
                    "caption": "The '🔄 Force apply' button calls IPS_ApplyChanges() directly, without you having to change anything in the form first – handy after a module update if the tile does not pick up the new code on its own."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "Label",
            "caption": "Standalone traffic-light tile for StromGedachtWidget."
        },
        {
            "type": "Label",
            "name": "SourceStatus",
            "caption": "Detecting data source ..."
        },
        {
            "type": "SelectInstance",
            "name": "SourceInstance",
            "caption": "Data source (empty = detect automatically)",
            "onChange": "SGWTILE_OnChangeSource($id, $SourceInstance);",
            "validModules": [
                "{D5A8C3A1-2222-4A55-8888-123456789003}"
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "CheckBox",
            "name": "AdoptWidgetName",
            "caption": "Take over the tile name from the source automatically"
        },
        {
            "type": "ExpansionPanel",
            "name": "PanelColors",
            "caption": "🎨 Traffic-light colors",
            "items": [
                {
                    "type": "SelectColor",
